# Known bugs of the guide scripts, found by tools/check-container-image and waiting for Phase 1.
# Columns, separated by a tab:
#   id | pattern | what is wrong | OS majors (optional: "10" or "8,9"; empty means all) | package the image needs (optional)
# The pattern is an awk regular expression, matched against a leftover line such as
# "M /etc/fstab", "unit crond.service enabled" or "cmdline missing console=tty0". A dash means
# that the check finds the bug in code. A bug that is observed and not listed fails the run.
# So does a listed bug that is no longer observed on an image it applies to: delete its line in the
# change that fixes it.
console-tty0-not-restored	^M /(boot/loader/entries/|etc/kernel/cmdline)|cmdline missing console=tty0	01-grub-bootloader --rollback does not put back console=tty0, which --apply removes on bare metal
no-rollback-02	^. /etc/(sysctl\.d/91-lowlat-rt\.conf|systemd/system\.conf)|irqbalance	02-cpu-isolation has no --rollback: it prints its usage and changes nothing
no-rollback-04	/run/fake-ethtool/	04-network has no --rollback: NIC settings stay as applied until the next boot
no-rollback-07	limits\.d/90-lowlat|/etc/tuned/	07-os-hygiene has no --rollback: limits, tuned profile and tuned state stay
runtime-unit-left-enabled	lowlat-runtime\.service	apply-all has no --rollback: lowlat-runtime.service stays installed and enabled
virtio-irq-false-pass	-	verify-tuning passes the IRQ line of a virtio NIC that no guide placed
rhel10-no-system-conf	-	02-cpu-isolation --apply fails on RHEL 10: /etc/systemd/system.conf does not exist there (the file is in /usr/lib/systemd)	10
tuned-profile-dir-rhel10	-	07-os-hygiene writes the low-latency profile to /etc/tuned/low-latency, but tuned on RHEL 10 reads /etc/tuned/profiles: tuned-adm rejects it and apply-all stops (the fake tuned-adm has the old layout too)	10	tuned
